WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.769
-Last time you were here, you
were a solo host on your show.

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
You did not have
a permanent co-host,

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now you have
Mr. Ryan Seacrest.

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:07.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Congratulations.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you very much.
-Are you --

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:10.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, give it up for Ryan,
everybody.

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.078 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:13.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it nice to have
someone permanent?

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you basically
would just -- you would be --

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
You would cycle
through guest hosts.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've guest-hosted.
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.620
-And you have to be the host not
just of the guests on the show,

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you also have to kind of,
like, help the co-host.

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:26.626 size:81% position:41%
-Well, first of all,
Ryan is like my dream.

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:28.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's been a friend of mine
for 15 years.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's nice to go to work
with your friends.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.932 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's great.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:33.533 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But it's weird.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:38.338
I would find myself constantly
being terrified of getting sick

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:40.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
or falling ill
or getting near --

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
If somebody coughed
on the street,

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would hold my breath
for 10 seconds.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:47.447
Because as you know, 10 seconds
is as long as it takes

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.448 size:84% position:42% line:92%
for germs to evaporate.

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:51.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A cough --
A cough only lives 10 seconds.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:51.551 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:55.188
A sneeze on the subway
is like 45 seconds to a minute.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:55.822 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And you're like...

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:57.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think currently
on the New York subway,

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:58.892 line:92%
sneezes are living 45 minutes.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Probably they could,
they could.

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:04.664
And then I would find myself
constantly worrying about,

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:06.066 line:92%
you know, knowing everything.

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:09.369
Not everything -- I just mean
knowing who the guests were

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:10.437 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and what time it was

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:14.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how many seconds
three minutes are in real --

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:15.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know what I mean?
-Yeah.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have to really host
a talk show to know,

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:19.012 size:84% position:42% line:92%
do I ask this question,

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:21.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
or is this long-winded person
going to give me a --

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:22.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely.
That's a big part of it.

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:25.251
Because someone is telling you
how much time you have left.

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
Right, right.

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:29.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so it was weird, because
I feel like you were --

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:30.123 line:92%
the show was like a child,

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.692 size:84% position:42%
and you had a different
co-parent every day.

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:33.493 line:92%
-And a different co-parent.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:36.896
-And they would show up and say,
"Is he allergic to nuts?"

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:37.931 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:38.598 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-You'd be like, yes.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:41.034 size:84% position:42%
-"What are we taking
to the school potluck?"

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:43.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, this is very exciting.
-Yeah, it's nice.

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:45.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, you had many co-hosts.
-Yes.

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:46.339 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-And I've done it.

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:48.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
Fred Savage, who's
our next guest, has done it.

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:49.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
Fred Savage has done it.

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:52.045 line:92%
-In 2006, you had a co-host.

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:54.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was a very famous
television star at the time.

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:56.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's now President
of the United States.

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:56.950 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm just curious,
how was he as a co-host?

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're welcome, everybody.
-Yeah.

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.789 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You're welcome.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.624 line:92%
He was great as a co-host.

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:05.625 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You know what's crazy?

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:09.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was talking about
running for president then.

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:10.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Then.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:13.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I remember actively having
this conversation with him.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:18.538
I said -- He said, "Everybody
wants me to run for president."

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:20.140 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-And I said, "Who?"

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.574 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:23.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was like,
"You know, everybody,

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:26.012
because I know, you know,
I'm good with dealing --

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:28.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
all of my business dealings,
I'm a negotiator."

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "But why would you
want to do that?

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.653
Why would you want to give up
your life, which is so good?

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:35.855
You're not going to be able
to go to Florida anymore.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:38.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're not going to be able
to golf every weekend."

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:40.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-And I was wrong.

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:43.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, you can do that.
-Yeah.

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:44.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were --
-Yeah.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:46.466 line:92%
-In principle, you were right.

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:47.167 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-In theory, I was right,

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:51.337
but now I realize that I'm an
idiot and none of that is true.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I will say,
if there's anyone

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:55.542 size:75% position:38%
who has made me feel
like an idiot more,

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:57.477
it is this gentleman right here,
because --

00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:58.378 line:92%
-He proves you wrong every time.

00:02:58.378 --> 00:02:59.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He proves you wrong
all the time.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, every time.
-But he was a good host?

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:02.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
He wasn't, like, nervous
or anything?

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
He wasn't like,
"I hope I was okay today."

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:05.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, he was a great --
No, he was --

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
He came out, and he was like,
"This is going to be

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:10.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
the biggest-rated show
you ever have in your life."

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "Oh, my God.
That's amazing."

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:15.662
-You guys always do fantastic
Halloween costumes on the show,

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.263 line:92%
and you trumped it up this year.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:19.265 line:92%
-I trumped it up, yes, I know.

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:21.267
-Did you hear from him?
Did you get any feedback?

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:26.139
-I didn't get any feedback from
him, which I was thankful for.

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:28.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because -- Because after,
you know,

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:30.310 line:92%
I heard that there was problems

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:34.013
with Melissa McCarthy's
portrayal of Sean Spicer,

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:35.582 line:92%
and I heard life became hard

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:37.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
because a woman
was portraying him,

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:39.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then I was like,
"Oh, my gosh,

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:42.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
if he finds out
a woman portrayed him,

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:43.523 size:88% position:44% line:92%
what's going to happen?"

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:45.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then I realized,
like, I mean,

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:47.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
I'm like Peter Pan at best.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.361 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So I guess I --

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.430
I guess he didn't have to
fire himself over that.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.166
-Yeah, he got it, he got it.
He survived -- He survived that.

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:54.968 line:92%
-He survived me playing him.

